      "review_state": "published",
      "description": "\"AMITERNUM, a town of the Sabines, in Italy, now extinct. The ruins are to be seen on the level ridge of a mountain near S. Vittorino and the springs of the Aternus; not far from Aquila, which rose out of the ruins of Amiternum.\" (Seally, 1787, Vol. 1, entry Amiternum)",
